    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ladies and Gentlemen,\n\nOn this important day, November 17, we gather to face an undeniable reality: the coal industry grows ever-present, choking our environment and stealing humanity’s hopes for a brighter, cleaner future. The air we breathe grows dirtier, and the earth beneath us weathers into ruin, all due to the relentless burning of our black gold. Coal is a relic of an outdated world, one that refuses to evolve despite the damage it causes—damage that we can no longer ignore.\n\nFriends, until the coal industry is silenced, the shadows it casts on our land, our water, and our skies will persist. But today, we stand as one voice demanding change, demanding immediate action to dismantle systems and policies that mandate our demise. We must reject this charade of progress and strive instead for a future fueled by the sun and wind, one that respects the integrity of our planet and our lives.\n\nLet us paint our massive courage upon the canvas of history, showing a united world that humanity will refuse to be terrorized by coal. Through passionate voices and unwavering resolve, standing together, we will build a path to justice, a world renewed by clean energy, and freed from the tyranny of coal. \n\nThank you,",
